WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.969
Large prompts need structure because the model has to distinguish task instructions from reference material.

00:00:06.969 --> 00:00:09.163
Start with a clear task statement.

00:00:09.163 --> 00:00:17.165
Explain what the model should do, what it should not do, what sources it should rely on, and what output format is expected.

00:00:17.165 --> 00:00:25.231
When many documents are included, the first section should help the model understand the job before it sees the raw material.

00:00:25.231 --> 00:00:27.296
Source organization is critical.

00:00:27.296 --> 00:00:31.362
Use labels, headings, delimiters, and consistent section names.

00:00:31.362 --> 00:00:38.654
Identify where each excerpt came from and whether it is authoritative, background, draft, example, or historical.

00:00:38.654 --> 00:00:46.784
If a prompt contains policy text, implementation notes, and user preferences, those categories should not be blended together.

00:00:46.784 --> 00:00:48.978
Clear boundaries reduce ambiguity.

00:00:48.978 --> 00:00:52.076
Priority ordering helps when material conflicts.

00:00:52.076 --> 00:00:54.980
Put controlling instructions before examples.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.690
Put current requirements before old notes.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:02.143
Put summaries before detailed appendices when the summary is trusted.

00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:11.241
Make constraints explicit: required tone, excluded topics, citation expectations, formatting rules, and assumptions that should be preserved.

00:01:11.241 --> 00:01:15.178
The model should not have to infer which source has priority.

00:01:15.178 --> 00:01:17.953
Requested output format should be specific.

00:01:17.953 --> 00:01:26.406
A large context prompt can ask for a table, decision memo, checklist, diff summary, risk register, or structured JSON-like outline.

00:01:26.406 --> 00:01:31.375
Specific formatting reduces wandering and helps reviewers inspect the result.

00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:38.151
The more material you include, the more helpful it is to tell the model exactly how to use that material.
